Package: netcfg
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: adduser, iproute2, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0
Recommends: wpasupplicant, hostapd, dnsmasq, iw
Suggests: avahi-daemon
Homepage: https://github.com/thanhnhu/netcfg
Description: web interface for configuring a headless Debian device
 netcfg drives Wi-Fi through whichever subsystem holds the radio
 (wpa_supplicant or NetworkManager) and IPv4/IPv6 through whichever backend
 manages the host (systemd-networkd, NetworkManager or ifupdown).
 .
 Every change that can cut the connection is applied with a rollback timer
 owned by the root agent, so a mistake restores itself instead of locking the
 operator out. When no network is left the device raises its own access point
 with a captive portal.
 .
 The package installs two static binaries: netcfgd, the privileged agent, and
 netcfg-web, the unprivileged HTTPS interface that reaches it over a Unix
 socket.
